/-!
# E.1: E-generation and the parameter n(G)

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, Section E.1, pp.209--214.

The source definitions, elementary tau and rank-bound properties, and existence
and quotient isomorphisms for minimal supplements are provided here. The full
inheritance theorem, quotient lifting, composition-factor reduction, and simple
group parameter values remain assembly obligations. A positive value of the parameter already supplies a generation witness and
the escaping E-member used in F.7.13. General existence of a positive bound
for every even-order group remains unproved; this file does not assert the
unfinished generation or classification results.
-/
